  triage:title "RULE-003 size cap: crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs production region is 1012 lines (mod tests at :1014), 12 over the 1000-line cap — pre-existing, not introduced by AV.3 fix-r5" ;
  triage:description "The production-region line count (raw lines before mod tests module) exceeds RULE-003 architectural cap of 1000 lines. File is at 1012 lines on develop and earlier AV branches (1013 lines starting with av1b-read-handler-cutover). This violation pre-dates phase AV, originating from AL.3 runtime-scaffold work. The lint (check_line_counts.py) counts only actual code lines (901 production code lines) and passes, but raw line count including comments and whitespace violates the architectural rule." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-av" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "architecture" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "deferred" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:deferredNote "quality-mgr ruling 2026-08-31 (QA-AV3 early-signal adjudication, fenix msg 01M1BMCBYZ30H3PB24XT5PHHZS): NOT-A-DEFECT-IN-PHASE-AV / deferred. The repo's mechanical authority for RULE-003 is check_line_counts.py max_production_lines=1000 applied to production CODE lines (blanks/comments excluded); the router counts 901 and passes. The 1012 figure is a raw-line reading that is not the enforced standard. Pre-existing since AL.3, present on develop. Phase-AM residual ControlPathSyncBridge deletion is expected to shrink this file. Do not dispatch a fix in phase AV; re-evaluate only if production code lines approach the 1000 cap." ;
  triage:deferredBy "quality-mgr" ;
